  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad, greeting.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Knowing this, that the trying of your faith worketh patience.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "But let patience have her perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, wanting nothing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "But let him ask in faith, nothing wavering. For he that wavereth is like a wave of the sea driven with the wind and tossed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For let not that man think that he shall receive any thing of the Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "A double minded man is unstable in all his ways.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Let the brother of low degree rejoice in that he is exalted:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But the rich, in that he is made low: because as the flower of the grass he shall pass away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "For the sun is no sooner risen with a burning heat, but it withereth the grass, and the flower thereof falleth, and the grace of the fashion of it perisheth: so also shall the rich man fade away in his ways.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Blessed is the man that endureth temptation: for when he is tried, he shall receive the crown of life, which the Lord hath promised to them that love him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Let no man say when he is tempted, I am tempted of God: for God cannot be tempted with evil, neither tempteth he any man:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "But every man is tempted, when he is drawn away of his own lust, and enticed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Then when lust hath conceived, it bringeth forth sin: and sin, when it is finished, bringeth forth death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Do not err, my beloved brethren.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Of his own will begat he us with the word of truth, that we should be a kind of firstfruits of his creatures.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Wherefore, my beloved brethren, let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "For the wrath of man worketh not the righteousness of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Wherefore lay apart all filthiness and superfluity of naughtiness, and receive with meekness the engrafted word, which is able to save your souls.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "For if any be a hearer of the word, and not a doer, he is like unto a man beholding his natural face in a glass:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "For he beholdeth himself, and goeth his way, and straightway forgetteth what manner of man he was.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth therein, he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "If any man among you seem to be religious, and bridleth not his tongue, but deceiveth his own heart, this man’s religion is vain.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:james:1:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Pure religion and undefiled before God and the Father is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, and to keep himself unspotted from the world.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "James 1:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:james:1:27"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
